    Don't let an untouched blank required field block unrelated metadata updates
    
    DublinCoreMetadataUtil.updateDublincoreCatalog() validated every
    required field in the collection, including ones the caller never
    touched. An event or series whose stored catalog already had a blank
    required field (e.g. title) therefore rejected every future update,
    even to a completely unrelated field, since the same untouched blank
    field failed validation every time.
    
    That blanket check was deliberately introduced to fix #6032 (silently
    creating an event/series without a title when no metadata was
    submitted at all), which relies on validating fields regardless of
    whether they were touched. Reconciles the two: the check in
    updateDublincoreCatalog() is scoped back to fields the caller actually
    touched, and the previous, unconditional check is split out into a
    new validateRequiredFieldsPresent(), called explicitly at the two
    creation call sites (event and series) where #6032's guarantee still
    needs to hold.
    
    Fixes #7920
    
